    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d358">

                <pb facs="0440" n="268" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg268"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/4084</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Haiti</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bailly-Blanchard</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-04-27T18:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 27, 1917, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your April 26, 3 p.m. Haitian Minister was informed that in eventuality mentioned
                    the United States would give “all proper assistance.” It is obvious that the
                    form this might take would depend upon circumstances and such necessities as
                    might arise, but generally speaking this Government would use every effort to
                    prevent Haiti from suffering injury as a result of her action.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
